<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4593" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auscultātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		ausculto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A listening</i>, <i>attending to</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auscultatio et publicorum secretorumque
					inquisitio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Tranq. 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An obeying</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Quid mihi scelesto tibi erat auscultatio?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 2, 6, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
